    "title_en": "Measurements of the branching fractions of $Λ_c^+\\toΛK^+ π^0$ and $Λ_c^+\\toΛK^+ η$ decays at Belle and Belle II",
    "abstract_en": "We present a study of the three-body, singly Cabibbo-suppressed decays $Λ_c^+ \\to ΛK^+ π^0$ and $Λ_c^+ \\to ΛK^+ η$ using data recorded with the Belle and Belle II detectors at the KEKB and SuperKEKB $e^+ e^-$ colliders. The data samples correspond to integrated luminosities of 980$\\,\\mathrm{fb}^{-1}$ and 570$\\,\\mathrm{fb}^{-1}$, respectively. We measure their branching-fraction ratios relative to the Cabibbo-favored decay $Λ_c^+ \\to Λπ^+ π^0$ as $\\mathcal{B}(Λ_c^+ \\to ΛK^+ π^0)/\\mathcal{B}(Λ_c^+ \\to Λπ^+ π^0)=(1.82 \\pm 0.07 \\pm 0.07)\\%$, with significantly improved precision compared to the previous measurement, and $\\mathcal{B}(Λ_c^+ \\to ΛK^+ η)/\\mathcal{B}(Λ_c^+ \\to Λπ^+ π^0)=(8.73 \\pm 0.35 \\pm 0.43)\\times10^{-3}$, corresponding to the first observation of the $Λ_c^+ \\to ΛK^+ η$ decay with a statistical significance exceeding 10 standard deviations. The first and second uncertainties are statistical and systematic, respectively. Using the world-average value of the branching fraction for $Λ_c^+ \\to Λπ^+ π^0$, we obtain the branching fractions $\\mathcal{B}(Λ_c^+ \\to ΛK^+ π^0)=(1.29\\pm 0.05\\pm 0.05\\pm 0.06)\\times10^{-3}$ and $\\mathcal{B}(Λ_c^+ \\to ΛK^+ η)=(6.20\\pm 0.25\\pm 0.31\\pm 0.30)\\times10^{-4}$, where the third uncertainty arises from the uncertainty in the world-average value of $\\mathcal{B}(Λ_c^+ \\to Λπ^+ π^0)$. The measured $\\mathcal{B}(Λ_c^+\\toΛK^+η)$ is significantly larger than predictions based on $SU(3)$ flavor symmetry.",
